0130: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0131:     """
0132:     Move aligned singleton markers along straight sightlines until they touch the nearest 2x2 block, leaving non-sightline and lower-left distractor markers fixed.
0133: 
0134:     Input structure
0135:     - The background is the dominant color.
0136:     - One foreground color forms filled 2x2 blocks.
0137:     - The other foreground color forms singleton marker pixels.
0138: 
0139:     Rule
0140:     - For each marker, find clear horizontal or vertical sightlines to any 2x2 block and choose the unique nearest block by travel distance.
0141:     - Move that marker to the adjacent ring cell on the same row or column of the chosen block.
0142:     - Markers with no clear sightline stay in place; a lower-row marker to the left of a block also stays fixed when that block already has chosen vertical markers both above and below it.
0143: 
0144:     Key insight
0145:     - The red 2x2 blocks act as magnets, so each direct marker ray is compressed to the one-cell ring around its nearest block while unrelated singleton markers remain noise.
0146:     """
